    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on leveraging volume and platoon advantages against middling rotations. Our strongest play is **Seiya Suzuki** (67.36), who benefits from a high-upside matchup against a sub-optimal pitcher; his score is buoyed by a significant +16% SP skill adjustment. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (64.27) and **Brice Turang** (64.10) anchor our production. **Brice Turang** is particularly vital today, as his high sprint speed and the opponent\u2019s slow delivery create a prime environment for a stolen base\u2014our most critical scarcity need. **Josh Naylor** (62.96) remains a set-and-forget core piece in the utility slot, providing high-floor production that we desperately need as we navigate a busy Friday.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the cut at 45.03. While his SP skill profile was favorable against an arm like Kay, the negative platoon impact of a L/L matchup and a lower spot in the order kept him on the bench behind the offensive potential of **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**. We are monitoring the risk factors closely; **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher test against Yamamoto, where his BvP history and the opponent's ability to hold runners have suppressed his score to 59.69. Furthermore, **Austin Riley** draws the short straw of the day, facing a tough outing against Cole, forcing us to rely on his park factor to keep his score in the marginal range. With **James Wood**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Mickey Moniak** all sidelined, our margin for error is slim, and we are proceeding with caution in the OF slots.",
